# TypeScript

Follow `packages/config/typescript/base.json`. Strictness stays on, including `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` and `exactOptionalPropertyTypes`.

- Import and export with ESM syntax. API and contract source import local files with a `.js` suffix.
- Put shared request and response shapes in `@velora/contracts` and infer types from Zod.
- Reject `any`. Use `unknown` at a trust boundary and narrow it.
- Handle rejected promises. Oxlint enforces `typescript/no-floating-promises`.
- Leave comments out. Choose names that carry the constraint.
- Keep formatting to Oxfmt and lint to Oxlint. Do not add ESLint or Prettier.
- Add a dependency only when the existing stack cannot do the job, and add it to the pnpm catalog when it is shared.

```ts
const row = rows[0];
if (row === undefined) {
  throw new Error("Expected a monitor row");
}
```
